# Build-Verify-Iterate Workflow Rule

## Description
Enforces a strict development workflow for the Living Truth Engine to prevent untested or unverified changes from being marked as complete.

## 🎯 Key Objectives
- Ensure every change is verified via bring-up → smoke → tests
- Prevent silent fallbacks and code/docs drift
- Keep changes small, reproducible, and observable

## 🧭 Workflow Overview
Every change — no matter how small — must go through this pipeline:
1. BUILD
2. VERIFY
3. ITERATE

---

## 1) BUILD
- Rebuild any container whose code was touched (especially `dashboard`).
- Commands:
```bash
docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml build dashboard
docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up -d dashboard
```
- Prove the running container has your changes:
```bash
sha256sum src/dashboard/unified_dashboard.py | tee /tmp/local_dash_hash.txt
DASH_CONT=$(docker ps --format '{{.Names}}' | grep -E 'dashboard|dash' | head -n1)
docker exec -i "$DASH_CONT" /bin/sh -lc 'sha256sum src/dashboard/unified_dashboard.py' | tee /tmp/incontainer_dash_hash.txt
diff -u /tmp/local_dash_hash.txt /tmp/incontainer_dash_hash.txt
```

## 2) VERIFY
- Health gates:
```bash
curl -s http://localhost:8050/api/health/full | jq .
```
All gates must return status ok before continuing.

- Tiny smoke run (limit=1, max_depth=1) on default channel from docs:
```bash
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8050/api/runs/youtube/start \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"channel_url":"https://www.youtube.com/@imaginationpodcastofficial","limit":1,"sort":"oldest","max_depth":1}' | jq .
```

- Verify bundle and corpus:
```bash
curl -s http://localhost:8050/api/runs | jq .
RID=<latest_run_id>
curl -s http://localhost:8050/api/runs/$RID | jq .
curl -s http://localhost:8050/api/runs/$RID/corpus | jq .
```
Expect `.veritasrun` folder, and files: `manifest.json`, `corpus.jsonl`, `merkle.json`, `metrics.json`; `corpus.jsonl` must contain ≥1 document.

- Tests (fail-fast):
```bash
pytest tests/test_no_fallbacks.py tests/test_health_gates.py -v
```

## 3) ITERATE
- If any step fails, stop and fix that step, then re-run from BUILD.
- When a step passes:
  - Update docs (`README.md`, `PHASE_*`, `CONSOLIDATED_COMPLETION_SUMMARY.md`).
  - Commit with message: `phaseX.Y: <brief change> [verified]`.
  - Paste bring-up & smoke outputs in PR under “Bring-up & Smoke evidence”.

## 🔒 Additional Constraints
- No hidden fallbacks; autosubs only if official fails and must be explicit in metrics and UI.
- Use only documented API endpoints; no direct container or DB calls.
- Responses respect envelope: `{status, data, error}`.

## ✅ Success Metrics
- 100% of changes tested end-to-end before “done”.
- No doc/code drift.
- Reproducible from fresh clone → bring-up → smoke → verified pass.